WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.370
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.500
the Kingdom of Chin launched an invasion
of the neighboring land of Gi.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.660
Ou Hon, Mou Ten, and Shin:

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.370
these bold soldiers and aspiring
great generals were together here now,

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.160
ready to usher in a brand-new age!

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.000
And that's why...

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.830
That's why I'm leaving when this battle is over.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.200
I don't know how many months,
how many years it will take,

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.580
but I <i>will</i> have my revenge.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:16.370
And once I have, when I come back here,

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:23.200
I think I should be able
to move forward with all of you.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.620
Let's win it, Kyou Kai.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.410
Yeah.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.160
Sanyou, the key position
holding down western Gi,

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.950
is home to four castle towns.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:53.750
West of those lay the Rui Plains.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.770
"Rui Plains"

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.830
Despite the name,
these plains are complex terrain,

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:02.620
encompassing mountains, forests,

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.950
and even swampland.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.870
Here, where one trades ease of movement

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.750
for the ability to enact myriad tactics,

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.200
was the site the unparalleled
martial master Ren Pa

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.330
had chosen for the decisive battle.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.910
Mou Gou--you've come!

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.120
I'm afraid I still don't quite understand...

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:34.040
I don't believe Mou Gou is
powerful enough to entertain my lord.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.330
No, not at all!

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.750
Mou Gou is the commonest kind of general.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.290
And yet,

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:47.910
he somehow has a lot
of campaigns under his belt.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.620
Ou Ki once told me:

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:58.370
In place of ability, Mou Gou
possesses powerful twin swords.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.290
Twin swords?

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:03.620
Seems Mou Gou's two
lieutenants are absolute monsters,

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.080
the likes of which the world has never seen.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:23.040
Well, then, Mou Gou...
let's see you swing them around,

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.080
these twin swords of yours!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:36.130
"Charge!"

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:58.290
Chin commanding general Mou Gou
and his army had arrived

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.620
at the Rui Plains,
site of this decisive battle.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.200
We have been waiting for you,

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.040
General Mou Gou.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.660
Fine work, you two!

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.870
What's with them?

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.580
Oh, right!

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.290
You don't know, do you.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.700
You again.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.750
Those are Grandfather's two lieutenants.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:49.790
Lieutenants?

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:56.000
General Kan Ki and General Ou Sen.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:02.120
Kan Ki and Ou Sen?
Never heard of 'em. Must not be that great.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.750
What are you talking about, Shin?
They're monsters--both of them!

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.200
Monsters?

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:12.370
In fact, most of
Grandfather's military successes

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.000
are thanks to them.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.750
Neither one is well-known as
a general because of... reasons.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.080
"Reasons," eh?

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.120
General Kan Ki was once
the head of a big band of robbers

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:30.040
whose territory was
the mountains of southern Chin.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:31.160
What?!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:35.540
He's a brutal man...
Even after being appointed general,

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:39.120
he can't shake the violent
temperament of his robber days.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.870
They say Kan Ki once took down a castle town

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:46.830
and beheaded all of its inhabitants himself.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:50.080
All of 'em?

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:51.700
Kan Ki the Headhunter.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:57.160
That name still follows him to this day.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:01.370
He's the worst kind of brute!
How'd he become a lieutenant, any--

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.120
Because he's a war genius.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.910
Back when he was a robber,
Chin sent out all kinds of punitive forces

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:13.290
to put a stop to his cruelty.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:18.250
But they never managed to
win out over Kan Ki's unique tactics,

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.790
strategies no one could ever have taught him.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:26.160
Yes, it was shameful
for Grandfather to take him on,

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:31.000
but even setting that aside,
his power more than makes up for it.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.830
So what about that Ou Sen general, then?

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:39.000
General Ou Sen is Ou Hon's father.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.000
Huh?!

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.910
And that means

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:52.080
he's the current head of the same
Ou clan that gave us Ou Ki.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:58.910
Head of the Ou clan... like Ou Ki...

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:02.000
Young sir! Hurry!

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.290
You got it! Coming!

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.790
Mou Ten, wait!

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:12.750
You said both those lieutenants had
"reasons". So what's Ou Sen's?

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:20.750
Ou Sen is the most dangerous man in Chin.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:25.950
He's been driven into the shadows
since the time of King Sho.

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.290
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.620
From what I hear, he has a certain ambition.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.120
Word is, he wants to be King.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.660
King?!

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:52.620
I'll be counting on you yet again, gentlemen...

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:57.660
Meanwhile, the Gi army
had also arrived at the Rui Plains.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:00.200
There, atop Baren San
and overlooking the main forces,

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:05.080
stood Gi's commanding general Haku Ki Sai!

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:13.080
Say <i>what</i> ?!

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.370
Our lord isn't the commanding general?!

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:17.580
I don't know this Haku Ki Sai--

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.040
Who the hell is he?

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.250
I believe he was one of the lieutenants

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:25.500
in General Go Kei's battle against Chin.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:31.120
Yes, the coward who turned tail
the second Ou Ki glared at him!

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:32.700
I'm not listening...

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:35.580
I am <i>not</i> listening--to <i>any</i> of it!

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:42.290
Well? Surprised, eh?

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.250
I'm glad I didn't say anything!

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:51.450
This is no laughing matter, my lord!
What's the meaning of this?

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:54.250
Why is <i>he</i> our commanding general?!

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:59.450
Reason number one: morale!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.500
Those in both Gi and abroad believe

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.160
I've been kept off the
battlefield these three years

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.370
for lack of the King's trust.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.580
My suddenly turning up as general

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.750
would hardly boost the Gi troops' morale!

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:14.830
Good point.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:18.790
But what's more, by using this man
with nothing to recommend him

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:21.450
but the inexplicable love
of his countrymen, this Chingen Sai--

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:24.040
Haku Ki Sai, my lord.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:28.200
I can pull the strings from the shadows!
It's much easier that way!

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.370
And, well... there are other reasons, I suppose.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:42.330
Ooh! You have a guilty conscience
because you still miss Sho?

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:43.790
Ow.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:48.620
Understood. If it is your decision,
my lord, we accept it gladly.

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:54.950
You do seem quite happy
to be on the battlefield again.

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:56.540
As do you all!

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.160
Haku Ki Sai!

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:04.910
Get over here! Time for the usual!

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.200
Woohoo!

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.500
"The usual"?

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.200
Kai Shi Bou!

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.200
Sir!

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:19.330
May fortune smile upon you!

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.580
And on you, my lord!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.870
Next, Rin Ko!

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:32.660
Aw, yeah! It's been so long!

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.330
May fortune smile upon you!

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:36.700
<i>That's</i> the stuff!

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:39.410
Next, Kyou En!

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:40.410
Sir!

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:51.200
Next! Gen Pou!

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.830
Ha! I think not.

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:57.910
Next! Haku Ki Sai!

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:00.620
N-No! I, er... I don't--

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.910
May fortune smile upon you!

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.160
The pain...

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:23.250
No--th-the heat!

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:26.700
What <i>is</i> this? This sensation? This...

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.660
this... <i>elation</i> ?!

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.500
I feel this power...
from the pit of my stomach...

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:40.450
Power welling up...

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:45.250
...all through me!

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:13.500
Now then, shall we get started?

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:14.500
Sir!

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:15.620
Sir.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:16.580
Sir!

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:17.580
Sir!

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.750
Take your positions!

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:29.990
"Ren Pa"

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:43.540
The enemy Gi army's
commanding general is <i>not</i> Ren Pa!

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.160
It is Haku Ki Sai!

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:49.500
Repeat: The enemy's
commanding general is Haku Ki Sai!

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:53.910
Ren Pa's not in charge
of this whole thing? What gives?

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:58.160
Mou Ten, sir... if it's not Ren Pa, then...

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:00.700
Things just got tricky.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:03.750
Now we can't count on Ren Pa
to be in the main force.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:16.790
Ren Pa...

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:21.290
No matter what moves you make,
I will be perplexed no longer.

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:27.080
I have strengthened my resolve!

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:35.250
Ou Sen, sir--a smoke signal
from the main camp:

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.580
"Good luck in battle," it says.

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:42.830
That's new...

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:45.620
Ol' Haku Rou is getting worked up for once.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:57.080
Ren Pa! It is I who shall have the last laugh!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:00.500
First unit, take the vanguard! Forward!

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:10.700
Here we go.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:13.370
Yeah...

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.910
Gyoku Hou Force, coming through!

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:20.500
Ou Hon...

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:24.790
So he got folded into the first unit, eh?

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:27.000
He's gonna get all the glory before us--again!

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:36.750
An ad-hoc thousand-man squad
in the first unit? That's rough.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:40.200
I'm sure that's a straw even
Ou Hon didn't want to draw.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:47.200
First unit, sir--you couldn't
ask for a better opportunity!

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:50.290
Let's show the Gi army and our allies both

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:53.040
the sheer might of the Gyoku Hou Force!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:55.250
Yes.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:58.200
And <i>him</i> as well.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:11.500
A message from General Do Mon
to all troops of the first unit!

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.250
This crucial first foray

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:15.030
"Do Mon, General of Chin"

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:16.040
will determine the direction of the war!

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:19.450
Use all your power to crush the enemy!

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.700
Rin Ko, sir,

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.580
we are prepared for mobilization.

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:33.660
Okie-doke!

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:47.290
It's so quiet. Will our army's
first unit be all right like this?

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.830
First unit!

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:08.120
Chaaarge!

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:11.450
Shall we?

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:04.200
Don't falter! Surround that
spearboy and take him down!

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:20.870
Uh-oh--the first unit is being forced back...

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.500
Shall I send in the second unit?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:26.910
No need to panic.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:32.410
This is when your Gi soldiers
<i>really</i> start to shine!

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:33.410
Huh?

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:40.000
The fifth unit will push in on the left.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:40.790
Sir!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:45.330
Seventh unit, head them off to the right.
Eighth unit, rush in there.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.500
Yes, sir!

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:51.410
Fifth unit, adjust formation!
Go left and strike the enemy!

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:57.620
Eighth unit, chaaarge!

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.000
Huh!

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:09.910
My lord was right: Gi troops are all business.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:14.870
I may be a stranger, but they still
follow my orders to the letter.

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:16.000
Quite commendable!

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:22.750
Okay... let's see, now...

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:26.540
I guess I ought to get started.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.540
Our army pushed them back!

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:43.830
And they're taking the offensive!

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.330
There he goes!

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:50.830
Rin Ko!

00:19:55.450 --> 00:20:00.080
General Do Mon! Thousand-man
commander Tai Un has been slain!

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.700
What?!

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:06.370
Tai Un's squad was one of those
temporary thousand-man units.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.830
So they weren't strong enough after all...

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:16.620
General! The enemy's elite unit
has attacked En Bi's squad,

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:19.580
and thousand-man commander En Bi has fallen!

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.660
<i>What</i> ?!

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:24.790
En Bi's squad was another
temporary thousand-man unit,

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.200
just like Tai Un's...

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:30.450
No!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.660
Is someone... targeting them?

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:37.330
The fourth unit is struggling!

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:41.200
Call back the second unit and
send them as reinforcements!

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:42.160
Sir!

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.750
The right garrison is being pushed back!

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:49.080
What's taking them?
Seventh unit, you're too slow!

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.620
The ninth unit has been captured at the rear!

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:52.910
What?!

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:58.200
The squad is moving slower
with these extra 700 troops--

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:02.080
slower than we're used to
with the Gyoku Hou Force.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:06.790
Shuu! Go help the ninth unit!
I'll protect Ou Hon!

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:11.250
The slower we move,
the more it'll take to tease open a seam...

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:17.870
These new soldiers are skilled,
but I knew they didn't measure up

00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:21.000
to the battle-bred 300 in the Gyoku Hou Force...

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:28.290
But I didn't know how much it would
hold us back, fighting beside them!

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:31.080
Ou Hon, sir! Lieutenant Ban You!

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:32.790
There's a new wave coming from the left!

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:34.410
From the left, too?!

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:37.580
Fine! Send the third unit after them!

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.080
But first, the right!

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:43.040
Get the right unit back
into formation, and quickly!

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:44.040
No...

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:46.750
...first this.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:49.160
Huh?

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:01.500
Look close, and you can tell
which squads are under command

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.660
and which squads aren't.

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:10.870
The former is strong, of course,
and the latter weak.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:16.580
And the weak squads in the
Chin army are my handiwork,

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:19.000
having assassinated all those commanders

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:22.830
and forced them to form temporary squads.

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:24.500
I see...

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:28.160
So you're the one who killed
our thousand-man commanders

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:29.290
at Kin Rikan.

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:36.700
And now I'll take <i>your</i> life...
Mr. Thousand-Man-Commander-For-A-Day.

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:38.370
Defend Ou Hon!

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:41.830
I wonder if you can!

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:44.080
Move.

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:47.450
S-Sir?

00:22:54.410 --> 00:22:55.620
I've got this.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:07.020
"Gen Pou's Cunning Scheme"
